    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21852370
    description: Concept DOI, resolves to the most recent version
repository-code: "https://github.com/papers-data/classroom-assignment-replication"
abstract: >-
  Institutional scheduling data from eight consecutive academic periods at the
  Tuluá campus of Universidad del Valle, the MiniZinc instances derived from it,
  the two-stage timetabling and room-assignment models, and the scripts that
  reproduce every table and figure in the accompanying article. Teachers carry
  labels local to this extract. The source scheduling system's own identifiers
  and the row-level surrogate keys are withheld, because that system's public
  endpoint returns them beside the teacher's name. The extract is pseudonymised
  rather than anonymous, and the README states the residual risk in full. No
  student-level data is included and no personal datum has been estimated.
keywords:
  - classroom assignment
  - university course timetabling
  - constraint programming
  - MiniZinc
  - benchmark instances
  - institutional data
